-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version], s 121 — the individual's rate of tax, in Part 7.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt.
--
-- WHAT THIS SECTION DOES. (a) taxes an individual's taxable income on a marginal scale of
-- 31%, 35% and 47%. (b)(1) replaces the 31% band of (a)(1), for income from personal
-- exertion and for all income of an individual who has reached 60, with a scale of 10%,
-- 14%, 20% and 31%; (b)(2) withholds those reduced rates from income for which books of
-- account had to be kept and acceptable books were not.
--
-- WHICH TAX YEARS IT ANSWERS: 2026 AND 2027 (NOTES.md, assumption A1). The figures printed
-- in the text carry the consolidation's own note that they are "adjusted for 2026-2027"
-- (src:4350), and s 120B(e)(1) fixes the amounts for 2025-2027, so no indexation intervenes
-- inside those two years. For 2025 and earlier the text of s 121 differed (its amendment
-- list ends with a 5786 amendment, src:4349, and the editorial tables show two ceilings
-- moving between 2024-2025 and 2026-2027) and that text is not in the sources. For 2028
-- onward s 120B(e)(2) restarts from the 1 January 2024 figures, which for the amended
-- ceilings the deposited text does not give, and the rounding Order is not encoded. Both
-- are declined by name. A caller who holds published ceilings for another year can still
-- use the rules below that take the ceilings as an argument.
--
-- NOT IN THIS MODULE: credit points (ss 33A-36A, row IL-01), which reduce the tax computed
-- here; the s 66 attribution of a couple's income (row IL-02); and every section that
-- charges an item at a rate of its own (an item so charged is simply not on this scale).

§ `Section 121 — the individual's rate of tax`
-- src:4347 | חלק ז׳: שיעורי המס
-- src:4349 | סעיף 121 – שיעור המס ליחיד [תיקון: תשכ״ה, תשכ״ו, תשכ״ח־2, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשל״ו־3, תשל״ח־2, תשל״ח־7, תשמ״א־8, תשמ״ד־9, תשמ״ז, תשמ״ז־2, תשנ״ד, תשנ״ה־6, תשנ״ה־8, תשנ״ו־6, תשנ״ז, תשס״ב־4, תשס״ב־9, תשס״ג־2, תשס״ג־4, תשס״ד־3, תשס״ד־7, תשס״ד־8, תשס״ה־9, תשס״ח־3, תשס״ח־12, תשס״ט־3, תשע״א־2, תשע״ב־2, תשע״ב־10, תשע״ג־2, תשע״ד־2, תשע״ז־6, תשפ״ו־6]

§§ `The figures the text prints, and the tax years they answer for`

-- src:4350 | (א) המס על הכנסתו החייבת של יחיד בשנת המס יהיה כלהלן: [note: (הסכומים מתואמים לשנים 2026–2027)]
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)(1)-(2) and (b)(1)(a)-(d) (source lines 4351-4358), stated by the note at source line 4350 to be adjusted for 2026-2027
GIVETH A `The income ceilings of section 121`
`the ceilings printed in section 121` MEANS
    `The income ceilings of section 121` WITH
        `top of the 31% band`              IS 301_200   -- (a)(1)
        `top of the 35% band`              IS 560_280   -- (a)(2)
        `top of the reduced-rate 10% band` IS  84_120   -- (b)(1)(a)
        `top of the reduced-rate 14% band` IS 120_720   -- (b)(1)(b)
        `top of the reduced-rate 20% band` IS 228_000   -- (b)(1)(c)
        `top of the reduced-rate 31% band` IS 301_200   -- (b)(1)(d)

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121, note at source line 4350; s 120B(e)(1) (source line 4344)
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the text prints the section 121 ceilings for tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
        `the tax year` AT LEAST 2026
    AND `the tax year` AT MOST  2027

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121 — amendment list at source line 4349; the text as it stood for tax years before 2026 is not in the deposited source
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text"

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 120B(e)(2) (source line 4345) restarts from the 1 January 2024 figures; the 5786 amendment of s 121 (source line 4349) moved two ceilings after that date; the s 120B(d) rounding Order is not encoded
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the section 121 ceilings from tax year 2028 are not determined by the deposited text` MEANS
    REFUSE "the section 121 ceilings from tax year 2028 are not determined by the deposited text"

GIVEN a              IS A TYPE
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN a
`section 121 does not answer in this model for tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    IF   `the tax year` AT LEAST 2028
    THEN `the section 121 ceilings from tax year 2028 are not determined by the deposited text`
    ELSE `section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text`

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121 (source lines 4350-4358)
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The income ceilings of section 121`
`the section 121 ceilings for tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    IF   `the text prints the section 121 ceilings for tax year` `the tax year`
    THEN `the ceilings printed in section 121`
    ELSE `section 121 does not answer in this model for tax year` `the tax year`

§§ `On each shekel — a marginal scale`

-- "על כל שקל חדש" — ON EACH shekel of a band, that band's rate: a marginal scale, not a
-- slab (phrasebook 3.6). A band "from 301,201 to 560,280" is read as the slice of income
-- above 301,200 and up to 560,280, on a continuous amount; nothing in the slice rounds the
-- income or the tax to whole shekels (NOTES.md, fork F16).
GIVEN `the income` IS A NUMBER
      `the bottom` IS A NUMBER
      `the top`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of` `the income` `above` `the bottom` `up to` `the top` MEANS
    max 0 (min `the income` `the top` MINUS `the bottom`)

GIVEN `the income` IS A NUMBER
      `the bottom` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of` `the income` `beyond` `the bottom` MEANS
    max 0 (`the income` MINUS `the bottom`)

§§ `121(a) — the scale`

-- src:4351 | (1) על כל שקל חדש מ־301,200 השקלים החדשים הראשונים – 31%;
-- src:4352 | (2) על כל שקל חדש מ־301,201 שקלים חדשים עד 560,280 שקלים חדשים – 35%;
-- src:4353 | (3) על כל שקל חדש נוסף – 47%.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)(1) (source line 4351)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate in section 121(a)(1)` MEANS 31%

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)(1)-(3) (source lines 4351-4353)
GIVEN `the taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `the ceilings`       IS A `The income ceilings of section 121`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(a) — the tax on` `the taxable income` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings` MEANS
         `the rate in section 121(a)(1)` TIMES (`the part of` `the taxable income` `above` 0              `up to` `the top of (1)`)
    PLUS 35%                             TIMES (`the part of` `the taxable income` `above` `the top of (1)` `up to` `the top of (2)`)
    PLUS 47%                             TIMES (`the part of` `the taxable income` `beyond` `the top of (2)`)
    WHERE
        `the top of (1)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the 31% band`
        `the top of (2)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the 35% band`

§§ `121(b)(1) — the reduced rates`

-- src:4354 | (ב)(1) על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א)(1) ובכפוף לאמור בפסקה (2), לגבי הכנסה חייבת בשנת המס מיגיעה אישית ולגבי הכנסה חייבת בשנת המס של יחיד שמלאו לו 60 שנים, יחולו שיעורים אלה:
-- src:4355 | (א) על כל שקל חדש מ־84,120 השקלים החדשים הראשונים – 10%;
-- src:4356 | (ב) על כל שקל חדש מ־84,121 שקלים חדשים עד 120,720 שקלים חדשים – 14%;
-- src:4357 | (ג) על כל שקל חדש מ־120,721 שקלים חדשים עד 228,000 שקלים חדשים – 20%;
-- src:4358 | (ד) על כל שקל חדש מ־228,001 שקלים חדשים עד 301,200 שקלים חדשים – 31%.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1)(a)-(d) (source lines 4355-4358)
GIVEN `the eligible income` IS A NUMBER
      `the ceilings`        IS A `The income ceilings of section 121`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(1) — the tax at the reduced rates on` `the eligible income` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings` MEANS
         10% TIMES (`the part of` `the eligible income` `above` 0         `up to` `top of (a)`)
    PLUS 14% TIMES (`the part of` `the eligible income` `above` `top of (a)` `up to` `top of (b)`)
    PLUS 20% TIMES (`the part of` `the eligible income` `above` `top of (b)` `up to` `top of (c)`)
    PLUS 31% TIMES (`the part of` `the eligible income` `above` `top of (c)` `up to` `top of (d)`)
    WHERE
        `top of (a)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 10% band`
        `top of (b)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 14% band`
        `top of (c)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 20% band`
        `top of (d)` MEANS `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 31% band`

§§ `121(a) and (b)(1) together — "notwithstanding (a)(1)"`

-- (b)(1) opens "notwithstanding what is said in subsection (a)(1)": the reduced rates
-- displace (a)(1)'s 31% for the eligible income inside the first band, and nothing else.
-- So the tax is (a) on the whole income, less (a)(1)'s rate on the eligible part of the
-- first band, plus the reduced rates on that same part.
--
-- WHERE THE ELIGIBLE INCOME SITS (fork F1). s 121 does not say which shekels of the scale
-- the eligible income occupies when an individual also has other income on it. Taken: the
-- eligible income occupies the bottom of the scale, so the "first 84,120 shekels" of
-- (b)(1)(a) are the first 84,120 shekels of the eligible income. The other readings (the
-- eligible income on top; pro rata) are in NOTES.md. Where the Ordinance does settle the
-- order, it puts special-rate income at the highest step (ss 91(b)(1), 125C(b): src 3347,
-- 4530); those items are not on this scale at all here.
--
-- THE TWO TOPS OF THE 31% BAND. (a)(1) ends at "the first 301,200" and (b)(1)(d) at
-- "301,200"; the text prints the same figure twice and never says which governs if they
-- part. If a caller supplies ceilings in which they differ, the rule declines.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)-(b)(1) (source lines 4351-4358)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`sections 121(a)(1) and 121(b)(1)(d) end the 31% band at different figures, and the text does not say which governs` MEANS
    REFUSE "sections 121(a)(1) and 121(b)(1)(d) end the 31% band at different figures, and the text does not say which governs"

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a)-(b)(1) (source lines 4351-4358); fork F1 (eligible income at the bottom of the scale)
GIVEN `the taxable income`  IS A NUMBER
      `the eligible income` IS A NUMBER
      `the ceilings`        IS A `The income ceilings of section 121`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121 — the tax on` `the taxable income` `, of which eligible for the reduced rates` `the eligible income` `, at the ceilings` `the ceilings` MEANS
    IF   `the ceilings`'s `top of the reduced-rate 31% band` EQUALS `the ceilings`'s `top of the 31% band`
    THEN       `s 121(a) — the tax on` `the taxable income` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings`
         MINUS `the rate in section 121(a)(1)` TIMES `the eligible part of the first band`
         PLUS  `s 121(b)(1) — the tax at the reduced rates on` `the eligible part of the first band` `at the ceilings` `the ceilings`
    ELSE `sections 121(a)(1) and 121(b)(1)(d) end the 31% band at different figures, and the text does not say which governs`
    WHERE
        -- At most the income itself, and at most the first band.
        `the eligible part of the first band` MEANS
            min (min `the eligible income` `the taxable income`) (`the ceilings`'s `top of the 31% band`)

§§ `The individual's income: what is on the scale, and what is eligible`

-- On the scale: every item of taxable income not charged at a rate of its own elsewhere.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(a) (source line 4350); s 1 "הכנסה חייבת" (source line 117)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income charged at the rates in section 121 of` `the individual` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `amount`)
             (filter (GIVEN i YIELD i's `charged at the rates in section 121`) (`the individual`'s `items of income`)))

-- "of an individual who has reached 60". Tested at the END of the tax year: an individual
-- whose 60th birthday falls on or before 31 December of the tax year (fork F2). Because the
-- tax year is a calendar year, that is the year of birth plus 60, and no leap-day case
-- arises.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1) (source line 4354); fork F2
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`aged 60 or more by the end of the tax year` `the individual` MEANS
    (DATE_YEAR (`the individual`'s `date of birth`) PLUS 60) AT MOST `the individual`'s `tax year`

-- src:4359 | (2) השיעורים המופחתים הקבועים בפסקה (1) לא יחולו על הכנסה שחייבים לגביה בניהול פנקסי חשבונות ולא נוהלו לגביה פנקסים קבילים.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1)-(2) (source lines 4354, 4359)
GIVEN `the item`       IS AN `An item of income`
      `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`eligible for the reduced rates` `the item` `, as income of` `the individual` MEANS
            `the item`'s `charged at the rates in section 121`
    ...     "(b)(1)" ... (   `the item`'s `from personal exertion`
                          OR `aged 60 or more by the end of the tax year` `the individual`)
    AND     "(b)(2)" ... NOT `the item`'s `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept`

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121(b)(1)-(2) (source lines 4354, 4359)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income eligible for the reduced rates of` `the individual` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `amount`)
             (filter (GIVEN i YIELD `eligible for the reduced rates` i `, as income of` `the individual`) (`the individual`'s `items of income`)))

§§ `Section 121 for an individual in a tax year`

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B`
`a problem with the items of income for section 121 of` `the individual` MEANS
    IF   any (GIVEN i YIELD i's `amount` LESS THAN 0) (`the individual`'s `items of income`)
    THEN JUST `an amount of income is negative`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The year is settled first, so that a year this model does not answer is declined in
-- return position rather than stored inside a RIGHT (phrasebook 11.8).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121 (source lines 4349-4359)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B` NUMBER
`the tax under section 121 for` `the individual` MEANS
    IF   `the text prints the section 121 ceilings for tax year` (`the individual`'s `tax year`)
    THEN CONSIDER `a problem with the items of income for section 121 of` `the individual`
         WHEN JUST `the problem` THEN LEFT `the problem`
         WHEN NOTHING            THEN RIGHT (`s 121 — the tax on` `the income on the scale` `, of which eligible for the reduced rates` `the eligible income` `, at the ceilings` `the ceilings printed in section 121`)
    ELSE `section 121 does not answer in this model for tax year` (`the individual`'s `tax year`)
    WHERE
        `the income on the scale` MEANS `the taxable income charged at the rates in section 121 of` `the individual`
        `the eligible income`     MEANS `the income eligible for the reduced rates of` `the individual`

§§ `Editorial notes after section 121 — inert`

-- The consolidation follows s 121 with two editorial notes: a link to the Tax Authority's
-- simulator, and a table of brackets for each year 2019-2027. Neither is law. They are not
-- encoded; the 2026-2027 table is used once, in the tests, as a second transcription of
-- the figures the text prints. Note that the table is not reliable as a source of figures
-- in its own right: its 2023 column misnumbers two band edges (116,711 for 116,761 and
-- 187,481 for 187,441, src:4419-4421).
